WEBVTT

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:37.610
<i>Why?</i>

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.290
<i>Why do you have to go so far for a fight?</i>

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:43.290
<i>That's right, Joe!</i>

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:44.650
<i>You lost to the champion, Tiger,</i>

00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:46.490
<i>and got KO'd by the first-ranked Harajima...</i>

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:49.800
<i>I can't believe you want to fight the No. 2, Nango!</i>

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:51.000
<i>It's fine, Nishi.</i>

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:56.850
<i>You and I have been fully in Joe's corner for a while now.</i>

00:01:57.510 --> 00:01:58.640
<i>We have to...</i>

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:02.890
<i>We have to stand by Joe, just for this match!</i>

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:19.070
No!

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:20.870
Hey, wh-what was that for?

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:23.870
How long are you gonna keep staring at that newspaper?

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:25.540
W-Well, aren't you interested?

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:29.130
I mean, if Bro Joe loses this match, he's not coming back to the gym!

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:31.340
So why don't you go cheer him on?

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:34.380
Bro Joe's out there training his butt off, you know!

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.300
Yeah, but...

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.880
It's too hard to watch him train.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:40.890
How do you think Bro Joe feels?

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:44.480
All right, already. I'll cheer him on.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:46.350
There's no arguing with you, is there, Sachi?

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:15.720
Don't worry about the body!

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:17.250
The temple! Go for the temple!

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:18.210
Damn!

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:22.130
That's no good! Even a baby could've dodged that!

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:23.090
What'd you say?

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:32.900
I felt that...

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:36.070
Yeah! That's the way!

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:36.070
<i>Way to go, Bro Joe!</i>

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:37.860
Joe hit the temple...

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.660
But what kind of punch was that?

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:42.200
He didn't even put his back into it!

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.780
It's no use. It's no use, Joe!

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:46.500
Joe! Keep up the pace!

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:47.870
Now, let's do it one more time!

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:49.290
Gimme all you got!

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:51.120
Okay, that's what I'll do, Nishi!

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:13.520
What? Joe's intensified his training?

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:17.020
Well, that's what the rumors say...

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:25.030
Never mind! Forget him!

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:27.320
He's just in his death throes!

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:30.210
If worse comes to worst, the referee is on our side.

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:32.000
Joe's like a moth drawn to a flame!

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:35.380
This Nango match will be his last time in the ring!

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:42.010
Of course, now that Yabuki is unable to hit the temple,

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:46.140
that damaged goods is destined to vanish from the ring sooner or later!

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:26.350
Yabuki's given us two disappointing fights in a row,
 against Tiger Ozaki and against Harajima,

00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:27.890
but he hasn't lost any spectators, has he?

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:31.230
Instead of losing spectators, he's actually gained some!

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:34.850
And there seem to be a lot of press here today, for whatever reason.

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:36.690
You think there's a reason behind that?

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:38.230
What do you think it is, old man?

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:41.860
There seems to be a different atmosphere in the arena today.

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:52.330
<i>Attention, all spectators, and viewers watching on TV!</i>

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:56.330
<i>I hate to be abrupt, but I'd like to take a little bit of your time.</i>

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:57.830
<i>Please, if I could have your attention.</i>

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:06.300
<i>Before the Yabuki-Nango match begins,
 I have big news for all Japanese boxing fans.</i>

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:10.010
<i>Currently sitting at the ringside in Korakuen Hall,</i>

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:12.180
<i>here on the invitation of Shiraki Gym,</i>

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:17.850
<i>we have a world-class boxer who's come all the way from Venezuela, South America.</i>

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:20.480
<i>He's the sixth-ranked bantamweight in the world...</i>

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:23.400
<i>Mr. Carlos Rivera!</i>

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:29.910
No. 6 in the world?

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:31.490
Carlos what?

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:32.580
I think he said "Rivera."

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:36.410
For a guy who's ranked top 10 in the world, I've never heard of him.

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:39.130
If he's a world-ranked fighter, you'd think we'd recognize his name.

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:39.840
But sixth-ranked?

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:41.340
Could be bogus information.

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:42.420
No, shouldn't be...

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:46.260
He just said he was here by invitation, but where is he?

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:49.930
You said it. How could he be here by invitation if there's no sign of him?

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:51.220
H-Huh?

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:54.890
Where did Mr. Carlos go?

00:06:55.730 --> 00:06:56.880
Now that's strange...

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:59.230
He was here just a second ago...

00:06:59.230 --> 00:06:59.900
Carlos!

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:01.310
Hey! Carlos!

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:02.400
Carlos!

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:03.820
Carlos!

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:16.410
How <i>elegante</i>. Very pretty. Beautiful.

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:17.620
My, Carlos...

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:19.460
Oh, there's his bad habit again.

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:22.420
He just can't resist himself around women.

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:24.710
You. You're pretty. Pretty! {I put the Engrish as it is, but it might work better to put it in Spanish (which I don't speak). Just a suggestion, I'll leave it to you guys to decide. ---SC}

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:27.000
Beautiful and charming.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.130
Carlos!

00:07:29.390 --> 00:07:32.930
Carlos, the ring announcer just introduced you.

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:35.600
Now, get in the ring and say a few words to everyone.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:37.940
Very well, Miss Yohko.

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:41.690
But I prefer the company of women to sweaty boxers.

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:43.060
What was that?

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:45.570
Oh, please don't glare at me with your wonderful eyes!

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:48.900
Your glare makes me very sad, Miss Yohko.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:50.780
Way to go, Sexy Sombrero Man!

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:53.910
Hey, now, are you that much of a skirt-chaser?

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:54.780
<i>You call yourself a world-ranked boxer?</i>

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:15.470
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:17.430
I'm Carlos Rivera!

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:20.520
The Terror of Venezuela! The Hungry Black Panther!

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:22.730
<i>Hey, that's enough of your nonsense!</i>

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:25.300
<i>It's not nonsense.</i>

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:28.990
<i>Mr. Carlos Rivera has won 34 straight fights since his debut,</i>

00:08:28.990 --> 00:08:31.740
<i>with 19 straight KOs.</i>

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:34.580
<i>Truly, he has a very terrifying record!</i>

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:37.260
Exactly!

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:40.580
Give me the chance, and I'll become world champion!

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:42.420
What do you think about that introduction?

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:46.960
Well, he may be world-ranked, but sixth-place isn't too noteworthy.

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:52.590
But come to think of it, I remember reading an 
article about him in an American boxing magazine.

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:58.020
Still, he kind of feels more like a Latin musician than a boxer.

00:08:57.760 --> 00:08:59.270
Thank you.

00:08:58.020 --> 00:08:59.770
He's got a very flamboyant aura.

00:08:59.270 --> 00:09:01.690
Thank you, everyone!

00:08:59.770 --> 00:09:01.680
You said it.

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:03.520
Hey! Carlos!

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:06.570
How long are you going to goof off?

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:08.360
You've got to wish the fighters luck!

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:09.490
Isn't that proper etiquette?

00:09:09.490 --> 00:09:12.530
Oh, it slipped my mind. I'm sorry.

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:15.530
Remember! It's proper etiquette to start with the higher-ranked fighter!

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:17.080
The one with the highest rank!

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:19.710
Yes, I understand. The highest-ranked fighter, no?

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:44.770
Carlos!

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:46.110
Hey, good luck!

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:47.560
I wish you the best.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:48.770
What's the matter with you, Carlos?

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:49.560
Get going!

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:59.570
No! The highest-ranked boxer's the one over there!

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:03.920
Th-That fucking...

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:06.080
Goddamn loopy bastard!

00:10:12.970 --> 00:10:14.300
Now, this is very strange.

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:17.670
I've never mistaken the highest-ranked boxer before.

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:19.680
That's a good one!

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:21.970
Goddammit! You wanna fight me instead!?

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:22.980
Forget about him!

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:25.650
Once the match is over, everything will go our way!

00:10:25.650 --> 00:10:26.480
But Coach!

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:27.680
I said don't!

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:29.320
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:31.570
Please don't be mad at me. Good luck.

00:10:31.570 --> 00:10:32.690
I wish you the best.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:38.700
What a nuisance, especially with such an important match ahead of us.

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.410
Yeah, but you gotta admit, he's a funny guy!

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:44.700
And I'd call it a good omen that he thought Joe was higher ranked than Nango!

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:46.790
Don't bother with that nonsense.

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:48.460
Just get me the Vaseline!

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:49.670
Here.

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:55.380
He didn't make a mistake!

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:57.760
He saw Joe's true colors!

00:10:58.340 --> 00:10:59.600
Do you understand, Joe?

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:05.890
He was... Carlos was able to see your inner glow as a fellow first-class boxer!

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:07.190
You got that, Joe?

00:11:07.190 --> 00:11:10.610
You have to live up to his sharp judgment!

00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:16.610
What's all this about?

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:18.860
I don't care if he's the sixth-ranked boxer in the world.

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:22.240
Putting on that farce before my match?

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:23.660
I don't need this!

00:11:51.990 --> 00:11:54.030
What's going on?

00:11:54.030 --> 00:11:54.960
Move out of the way!

00:11:56.780 --> 00:11:57.780
Hey, stop pushing!

00:11:57.780 --> 00:11:59.400
The match is about to start!

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:01.900
Hey, numbnuts! We're pushing <i>because</i> it's about to start!

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:03.490
What'd you call us!?

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:04.660
Shut up, already!

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:06.660
I can't hear the TV!

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:08.920
You want me to make mince meat outta you!?

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:15.540
<i>Now introducing the second-ranked bantamweight fighter, Nango Michiru of Ote Gym,</i>

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:17.670
<i>versus Yabuki Joe of Tange Gym!</i>

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:23.180
<i>Just earlier, Mr. Carlos Rivera mistook Yabuki Joe as being higher-ranked than Nango...</i>

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:25.180
That wasn't a mistake!

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:27.350
<i>But we'll have to see how the match turns out...</i>

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:29.810
<i>because the first round's about to begin!</i>

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:33.110
Go, Joe!

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:34.730
Don't lose, Bro Joe!

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:36.400
Go get 'im!

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:37.900
Don't lose!

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:38.730
Good luck!

00:12:50.210 --> 00:12:51.710
And there's another straight right from Nango!

00:12:51.710 --> 00:12:53.210
Nango's brimming with confidence!

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:54.540
He's off to a good start!

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:56.710
And Nango's left connects!

00:12:57.460 --> 00:12:58.700
And another left!

00:12:58.700 --> 00:12:59.840
Joe's on the defensive!

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:06.180
It seems he's utterly lost the wild nature that made him so vicious against all his other opponents!

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:17.270
Let's go home, Robert and Carlos.

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:19.060
You're leaving without watching the match?

00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:22.200
I don't need to see the results to know them.

00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:24.450
Yabuki Joe's going to have a third shameful loss.

00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:27.280
Third loss?

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:29.660
You're saying he's going to lose to Nango?

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:33.580
I was not lying when I said he was better than Nango!

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:36.340
You both seem to be quite confident in Yabuki.

00:13:36.340 --> 00:13:39.510
Fine, then. I'll stay with you two until you're both satisfied.

00:13:39.510 --> 00:13:42.090
No, it's fine, Miss Yohko.

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:42.550
But...

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:43.550
But what?

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:49.560
I've heard that this Yabuki killed your gym's fighter, Toru Rikiishi, in a match six months ago.

00:13:54.690 --> 00:13:59.820
Why don't you want to watch the full match of someone you have such history with?

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:00.650
Do you want to know?

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:09.990
Because he's not the same man he was back then.

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:11.490
Not the same?

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:14.040
Yes, back when he fought our Rikiishi-kun,

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:17.670
he was such a violent and intrepid beast, he was almost beautiful.

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:51.990
But now, his body acts up whenever he hits the temple.

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:54.290
He's no more than a pitiful stray.

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:58.830
He's become so miserable, I can't watch him.

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:17.100
Dammit...

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:23.810
Dammit!

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:27.570
Yabuki! Lift your head!

00:15:29.160 --> 00:15:31.820
I see. His movements are clumsy and awkward.

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:35.330
He couldn't even kill a fly like that!

00:15:46.550 --> 00:15:48.600
Referee! That was a foul!

00:15:48.600 --> 00:15:49.630
Take off points!

00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:57.100
Hey! Yabuki!

00:15:58.190 --> 00:16:00.140
Demerit! One demerit for Yabuki!{is an8 just for the count?}

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:09.490
The referee has given a wildly desperate Joe a demerit! This is not looking good!

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:11.370
This is looking to be an awful match!

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:14.950
You said it! His sloppy footwork, his wide-open defense...

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:17.950
I can't believe a man could change so much in such a short time!

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:20.250
What's your problem, Joe? I can barely stand to watch!

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:21.960
You're just fouling left and right!

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:25.170
That's not boxing! That's just brawling!

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:26.420
I want my money back!

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:27.670
You're an embarrassment to all boxers!

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.090
Just quit while you still can!

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:35.430
What's the matter, Bro Joe?

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:36.770
Get a grip, Bro!

00:16:36.770 --> 00:16:38.430
Well, don't just zone out!

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:40.150
You gotta cheer for him instead!

00:16:40.150 --> 00:16:42.020
Go! Punch him, Joe!

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:42.020
<i>Punch, Joe!</i>

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:42.680
Punch!

00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:44.690
I can't hear you!

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:47.690
Hit him, Joe! Hit him!

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:49.010
Hit him, Joe!

00:16:49.010 --> 00:16:51.010
We're right behind you!

00:16:51.700 --> 00:16:54.910
Yeah, go get him! What's the hold-up?

00:17:01.170 --> 00:17:03.200
Fine... If that's the way it's gonna be...

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:05.290
Just watch me!

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:12.670
Oh, he's done it!

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:15.130
Joe hit him!

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:26.350
All right! Yabuki's back on the offensive!

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:36.400
Nango! Hang in there!

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:42.410
Damn you, you bastard!

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:57.180
All right! He's down!

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:10.110
R-Rikiishi!

00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:15.990
Get to a neutral corner.

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:30.500
Oh, no! He's doing it again!

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:31.000
Joe!

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:35.800
Get up! Now's your chance to finish him off!

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:37.510
The son of a bitch is throwing up again!

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:40.470
Referee!

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:44.270
A-Aren't you gonna take the count?

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:46.220
Uh, right.

00:18:47.150 --> 00:18:49.310
I can't believe you screwed up the count.

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:52.360
If you hadn't messed up, I would've won by KO!

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:54.480
Don't tell me you're in cahoots with them!

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:57.490
Silence! Talking back to the referee is a foul!

00:18:58.070 --> 00:18:58.820
Gotcha!

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:00.120
Here!

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:09.080
Now! Hit him! Hit him!

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:36.650
Down! He's down!

00:19:36.650 --> 00:19:37.440
Get to the corner!

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:44.790
Joe!

00:19:44.790 --> 00:19:46.450
Get up, Joe!

00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:53.420
Let's go now.

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:55.470
You don't want to watch any more of this match, do you?

00:20:39.930 --> 00:20:42.300
Now that was an awful match!

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:44.260
<i>That was an absolutely ugly match!{switches to An halfway}</i>

00:20:44.260 --> 00:20:48.560
<i>Blood, sweat, vomit, and fouls flowed in the supposedly sacred ring!</i>

00:20:48.560 --> 00:20:50.060
<i>It's truly a dreadful display!</i>

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:52.020
<i>But the match is over.</i>

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:55.020
<i>Yabuki Joe's suffered a fatal third loss!</i>

00:20:56.070 --> 00:20:58.520
Stupid Joe! Why'd you have to lose?

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:02.530
What's gonna happen to him now?

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:13.830
Run along now. It's time to close the store.

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:15.050
Go home!

00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:49.950
